-- Two parameter names that a lossy sanitiser maps to one SMT-LIB symbol
-- (`a|b` and `a_b`). The audit of #784 found this proved; it is false at any
-- x that is not whole, as `l4 run` confirms at x = 0.5.
GIVEN `a|b` IS A NUMBER
      `a_b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`d1` `a|b` `a_b` MEANS `a|b` MINUS `a_b`

§ `Wrong proved`
    GIVEN x IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT `IS INTEGER` x OR (`d1` x 0 EQUALS 0)
